    content: "# Two kinds of role\n\n- **Platform role (Zebron staff):** a Zebron platform administrator has full access to every organization.\n- **Organization role:** each person has exactly one role in each organization they belong to.\n\n# The organization role ladder\n\nEach role includes everything the roles below it can do.\n\n1. **Member:** uses every application the organization has; opens personal support tickets.\n2. **Staff:** plus Test Center management (gear on the Test Center card) and Knowledge Center management (gear on the Knowledge Center card): write questions and articles.\n3. **Manager:** plus the Administration page: invite people, change roles below their own, dashboard banners, mailbox, Contract & Billing, organization support tickets, member profiles, and moderation of the organization's Community.\n4. **Administrator:** plus Organization Setup, Configuration and the Audit Log; can request application changes (the owner approves).\n5. **Owner:** plus approving requests, accepting the partner agreement, transferring ownership and terminating the contract.\n\n# Platform administrators\n\nA platform administrator sees everything. The dashboard badge shows **Platform Admin** for them even if their organization role is Member, which explains why a \"Member\" can sometimes see admin cards.\n\n> Changing a role: see \"Inviting people and changing roles\".",
