    category: "Courses",
    audience: ["all"],
    tags: ["courses", "learning", "lessons", "certificates"],
    content: "# Where to find courses\n\n- **Zebron courses:** open **Courses** from All apps (Work and learning), or go to **/courses**. The old Learning Lab address (/learning) now opens Courses.\n- **Your organization's courses:** open **Courses** in your organization's app menu. You see your organization's own courses first, then Zebron's.\n\nAnyone can browse the catalog. **Sign in** to start a course and save your progress.\n\n\n# Programs in the catalog\n\nCourses that belong to a **program** (such as the Cybersecurity Program or the ServiceNow Administrator Program) are shown together at the top of the **Catalog** tab, in step order:\n\n- Each program shows its number of courses, total time, levels and your progress (\"3 of 8 completed\").\n- **Start with step 1** or **Continue: step N** opens the next course you have not finished.\n- A tick marks completed steps; the arrow on the right hides or shows a program's list.\n\nOther courses follow under **More courses**. Searching or picking a topic shows a single list, with program courses labelled \"Program · Step N\".\n# The three tabs\n\n| Tab | What it shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| **My learning** | A **Continue** card for the course you used last, your week, courses in progress and recommendations |\n| **Catalog** | Every published course. Filter by topic or search by course name or skill |\n| **Certificates** | Every course you have completed |\n\nOn phones, tap the **search icon** in the header to show the search bar.\n\n# Taking a lesson\n\n1. Open a course and press **Start course** (or **Resume**).\n2. Read the lesson, watch the video or listen to the audio. Videos, audio and slides play inside the lesson; links from other sites open in a new tab.\n3. Answer the **quick check** at the end. **Complete and continue** unlocks once you choose the right answer. A wrong answer just asks you to try again.\n4. Your progress is saved when you continue. The next unfinished lesson opens.\n\nThe outline on the left (wider screens) shows which lessons are done.\n\n# Your week\n\n- **Week streak:** weeks in a row with at least one completed lesson. The dots show which days you learned this week.\n- **Minutes this week:** the length of the lessons you completed, against a goal of 60 minutes.\n- **Completed** and **Skills earned** count finished courses and their skills.\n\n# Certificates\n\nWhen you finish the last lesson your certificate opens. It shows your name, the date, your average first-try score on the quick checks, the skills and a certificate code.\n\n- **Print or save as PDF** uses your browser's print window (choose \"Save as PDF\").\n- **Add to LinkedIn** opens LinkedIn's \"Add licence or certification\" form, filled in.\n\n> Your score counts only your **first** answer to each quick check, so take your time.\n\n# Zebron Learning\n\nCourses and the Test Center together make up **Zebron Learning**. The Courses tabs include **Test Center**, and the Test Center quiz library links back to **Courses**.\n\n# The end of a course\n\nAfter the last lesson the **course summary** opens: lessons done, time spent, your first-try quick check score, what you learned and the modules you covered.\n\n- If the course has a **final exam**, press **Take test**. The exam shows its rules first (questions, pass mark, time limit, attempts), then one question at a time with a question map and, when set, a timer that submits by itself.\n- **A certificate needs a passed final exam.** Courses without an exam can be completed but give no certificate.\n- Failed? The result shows your score by topic and the questions to review. Use **Try again** if attempts are left.\n\n# Checking a certificate\n\nEvery certificate has a code such as ZB-7Q4K-M2XP. Anyone (for example an employer) can check it at **/verify**: it shows the name, course, date and exam score.",
