    summary: "Who can build courses, how to use the course builder, which video, audio and slide links play inside lessons, and how publishing works.",
    applicationKey: "platform",
    contentType: "how-to",
    category: "Courses",
    audience: ["admin", "support"],
    tags: ["courses", "course builder", "video", "publishing"],
    content: "# Who can build courses\n\n| Courses | Where | Who |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Zebron courses** (everyone) | /courses/manage, or **Courses** on the admin dashboard | Platform administrators |\n| **Organization courses** (members only) | **Manage courses** tab on your organization's Courses pages, or the gear on the **Learning** card | Staff write and submit; managers, admins and owners publish |\n\nThe **Manage courses** tab only appears for people who can use it. It lists every course, drafts included.\n\n# Review (organization courses)\n\n| Status | Who changes it | Learners see it |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Draft** | Staff and above | No |\n| **In review** | Staff press **Submit for review**; a manager presses **Approve and publish** or **Send back** (with a note the author sees) | No |\n| **Published** | Managers and above | Yes |\n\n- Staff cannot change a published course: ask a manager to edit it or move it back to draft.\n- Managers see **Waiting for your review** at the top of Manage courses, and a number on the Learning card's gear.\n- A submitted course can be taken back with **Withdraw from review** (⋮ menu).\n\n# Learning administration\n\nWith Courses and the Test Center, the gear on the dashboard's **Learning** card opens one page with a card for each: published, draft and in-review courses; quizzes and published questions; and links to Manage courses, New course, Test Center settings, Questions and Learner results. With only the Test Center, the gear opens its settings.\n\n# Create a course\n\n1. Press **New course**. It starts with one module and one lesson.\n2. **Course details:** title, a one-line summary (shown on the card), \"About this course\", topic, level, what learners will be able to do (one per line), skills (separated by commas) and a cover colour.\n3. **Outline (left):** rename modules by typing in their title, **Add lesson**, **Add module**, and use the arrows to reorder. Moving a lesson past the end of a module moves it into the next one.\n4. **Lesson:** select it, give it a title and the minutes it takes, then add blocks.\n5. Press **Save draft** (or Ctrl+S). Leaving with unsaved changes asks first.\n\n# Blocks\n\n| Block | Use it for |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Text** | The lesson itself. Supports **bold**, *italic*, # headings, lists, links and tables |\n| **Video** | A video link, with an optional start time (for example 1:30) and caption |\n| **Audio** | A podcast episode or audio file |\n| **PDF or slides** | Slides or a document shown inside the lesson |\n| **Image** | An https image link, with a description for screen readers |\n| **Tip** | A highlighted tip |\n| **Quick check** | A question with 2–6 answers; mark the right one and add why it is right |\n\nUse the arrows on each block to reorder it, and the bin to delete it.\n\n# Which links play inside the lesson\n\nPaste the link and the builder tells you straight away, with a preview.\n\n- **Video:** YouTube, Vimeo, Loom, Google Drive, Microsoft Stream (use Stream's **Embed** link), or a direct .mp4 / .webm file.\n- **Audio:** SoundCloud, Spotify (episodes, shows, tracks), or a direct .mp3 / .m4a file.\n- **PDF or slides:** Google Slides, Google Docs, Google Sheets, or a PDF stored in Google Drive.\n- **Anything else** (including a PDF on another website) shows a button that opens it in a new tab.\n\n> Sharing settings still apply: a Google Drive file or Slides deck must be shared so learners can open it (for example \"Anyone with the link\").\n\n# Publishing\n\n- **Publish** makes the course visible to learners. The **Before you publish** list shows what is missing: a title, at least one lesson, content in every lesson, complete quick checks and https links.\n- A published course is **live**: **Save changes** reaches learners immediately.\n- **⋮ → Unpublish** moves it back to draft; **⋮ → Delete course** removes it and its lessons for good.\n- **Preview** opens the saved course as a learner sees it.\n\n> Deleting a lesson that learners have finished does not change their percentage until they complete another lesson.\n\n# Final exam\n\nIn **Course details → Final exam and certificate**, switch the exam on and choose a **Test Center quiz** (Zebron's, or your organization's own), then the number of questions, pass mark, time limit and attempts. Questions are drawn at random from the quiz's published questions and **graded on the server**; learners see their score and topics to review, never the answers. Without a final exam a course gives no certificate.\n\n# Grouping courses into a program\n\nIn the course builder's details, fill in **Program (optional)** and its **Step**. Every published course with the same program name is shown together in the catalog, ordered by step. Leave the program empty for a standalone course.",
